# Character reference photos

## Location
- Canonical folder: `lessons/assets/refs/george/`
- Full tag index: `lessons/assets/refs/george/CATALOG.md`
- Photos are **private / gitignored**; only `*.md` catalogs are committed
- New raw drops go in `ref/` (see `ref/README.md`), then rename into the canonical folder

## Cast ids (use these names in filenames and story art)
- `george` — boy ~5, lesson hero (short black hair with bangs, round face)
- `daddy` — father (short dark hair, usually thin glasses)
- `mummy` — mother
- `sylvia` — older sister (often cap / ponytail)

## Filename pattern
`{subjects}-{setting}-{pose-or-mood}[-variant].jpg`  
Example: `george-daddy-outdoors-lifevest-smile.jpg` (George listed first)

## When generating lesson illustrations
1. Open `CATALOG.md`, then **Read** the chosen photo(s) before drawing
2. Default George likeness: `george-solo-bed-smile.jpg` (`priority: primary`)
3. Match cast + mood tags from the catalog to the story beat
4. Keep George consistent across the whole lesson; do not invent a different child face
5. Never embed these private photos in published HTML; only AI/drawn picture-book art goes under `lessons/assets/lesson-XX/`
